  "question": {
    "text": "A 400 g solid cube having an edge of length 10 cm floats in water. How much volume of the cube is outside the water ?\n(Given : density of water $=1000 \\mathrm{~kg} \\mathrm{~m}^{-3}$ )",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "QrUAq",
      "text": "$1400 \\mathrm{~cm}^3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IrRAv",
      "text": "$600 \\mathrm{~cm}^3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "75GBm",
      "text": "$4000 \\mathrm{~cm}^3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "63C2z",
      "text": "$400 \\mathrm{~cm}^3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Volume of cube inside water\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\left(\\frac{\\text { Denslty of cube }}{\\text { Denslty of water }}\\right) \\times \\text { Volume of cube } \\\\\n& =\\frac{\\text { Mass of cube }}{\\text { Denslty of water }} \\\\\n& =\\frac{400 \\mathrm{gm}}{1 \\mathrm{gm} / \\mathrm{cm}^3} \\\\\n& =400 \\mathrm{~cm}^3\n\\end{aligned}$\nVolume of cube outside water\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\text { Volume of cube }- \\text { Volume of cube inside water } \\\\\n& =1000 \\mathrm{~cm}^3-400 \\mathrm{~cm}^3 \\\\\n& =600 \\mathrm{~cm}^3\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
